.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:66: ## Cross-cutting C — GitHub-style project activity UI (mimic) (serves REQ-010, REQ-011)
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:68: Design intent: model the project page and the in-progress card on a code-host's repo view (GitHub's "About" sidebar + activity graphs) so contributors and the public read a project's health at a glance. `[intent]`
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:71: - **Languages/stack bar** — a horizontal colored percentage bar of the repo's languages (GitHub `/languages`); colored language dots on cards.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:73: - **Activity sparkline** — a mini weekly bar graph, GitHub Pulse/Commits-style.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:75: - **Contributor** — the single assigned volunteer's avatar (GitHub shows a contributor grid; ai4good is single-dev).
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:77: - **Readiness %** `[deferred → RM-62]` — modeled on GitHub's Community Standards checklist → ai4good completion-readiness (README, RUNBOOK, deploy instructions, ≥1 passing CI run, LICENSE, live URL). Not a v1 gate; the checklist ships with the formal completion ceremony.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:84: **Open vs in-progress (load-bearing):** GitHub activity stats need a repo with history, and ai4good repos exist only from kickoff. So the **open-project listing card** = static attributes only (no repo yet); the **project page + in-progress showcase card** = the activity panel above.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:86: **API sources (public, no auth for public repos):** `/repos/{o}/{r}` (pushed_at, license, primary language), `/languages`, `/stats/commit_activity` + `/stats/contributors` (202-cache-then-fetch), `/community/profile` (readiness). **PM task progression comes from the Linear mirror, not GitHub.**
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:103: - **Add connectors** — `add_connector` only returns a dashboard **deep link**; GitHub + Stripe connector setup stays a Lovable UI step.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:117: - **Connector catalog (confirms UI-only add).** Zero-config (Lovable's built-in type): **lovable-cloud, supabase, stripe, paddle, shopify, ai_gateway**. Standard (OAuth/APIKEY): **github (API), linear, salesforce, hubspot, twilio, resend, …**. MCP: linear, notion, sentry, posthog, atlassian, figma, …. All `is_enabled` in the catalog, but `add_connector` only returns a **dashboard deep-link** — programmatic add still not possible. GitHub two-way **sync** is a workspace feature (`experimental_features.gitsync_github`), separate from the GitHub-API connector.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:161: ### REQ-008 — GitHub integration
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:164: - The Lovable→GitHub setup as an **11-step auto-validated checklist**; aging escalation.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:165: - `[verify]` Lovable's GitHub App creates the repo where pointed and its collaborator permissions do **not** propagate to GitHub.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:191: - `[deferred → RM-62]` formal ceremony: disabled-button-with-instructions when the repo doesn't exist; live-URL capture via a completion form as the sole gate; sign-off / acceptance flow + rejection loop; the guided-maintenance ritual — (i) enable row-level access enforcement on the Lovable DB (off by default — PII footgun); (ii) demo chat/plan-mode + checkpoint rollback; (iii) set a Lovable spend cap; (iv) confirm two-way GitHub sync; the 30-day-alive automated ping.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:207: - Setup checklist (workspace + Lovable project creation, invites, GitHub-sync, paste-back, auto-validation).
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:209: - **Role model (verified against Lovable's full workspace role matrix, 2026-07-13).** From the matrix: *Create new projects in a workspace* = Editor **Yes**; *Manage Supabase* (enable/manage the DB) = Editor **Yes**; *Manage GitHub* = Editor Yes; *Publish* = Editor Yes; *Manage plans & billing* = Editor **No**; *Manage Integrations* (workspace-level connectors) = Editor **No**; *View usage* = Editor **No**. Only *Disconnect Supabase* (destructive, project-level) is admin/owner. So the volunteer is invited as **Editor** and does the **entire technical setup**; the NGO's role collapses to account/billing. (The PRD states these as capabilities — "build-only member with no billing access", "read-only monitoring account with no billing or admin access" — the verified Lovable mechanism for both is the **Editor** role; d56.) Kickoff split:
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:211: - **Volunteer (Editor):** **create the project, enable its database**, **connect GitHub** (repo → platform org), inject conventions + reviewer skill, build, publish, consume credits — never touches billing.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:220: - `[open]` **repo location.** REQ-008 places the repo in the **platform GitHub org**; connecting Lovable to a platform-org repo requires the volunteer to hold create/connect rights in that org (the Lovable GitHub-App install is an org-admin action). Alternative: repo in the **NGO's own GitHub** removes the platform-org GitHub-access dependency (NGO/volunteer wire it unaided) but relocates the public-only + visibility guard (REQ-008) to per-repo checks. Decision pending — does not change REQ-008 yet.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:243: - `[verify]` free-tier Linear events, API mutations, programmatic invites, rename, pre-connected GitHub integration seeing later repos. Fallback: paid tier or git-based state with a deterministic truth layer.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:255: - v1 controls = **GitHub secret scanning + push protection** org-wide; founder break-glass repo-hide (emergency takedown).
