.taskmaster\docs\prd.md:294: - [ ] **At first project application** (same first-commitment-moment principle as the GitHub link gate per REQ-007), volunteer must explicitly accept the relevant ToS + Platform Promise clauses: *"ai4good is a limited, bona-fide coordination layer — no one is obligated to deliver a specific outcome, and my participation is governed by ai4good's Terms of Service. I am volunteering my time (not an employee or contractor). All my work on any project I'm matched to will be public-by-default open-source under MIT (private allowed by NGO justification per Platform Promise §2). I will use each project's Anthropic API key only for that project's work — not for personal projects, other ai4good projects, or any non-project purpose. When a project handles real data, I will only work with the synthetic/anonymized fixtures the NGO provides (Tier-2 special-category data, REQ-004), and I will keep what I see confidential. Violations may result in account suspension and forfeiture of completion credit."* Bumping the ToS/disclaimer text version re-triggers acceptance. Acceptance is a property of the volunteer account (`volunteer_profiles.first_apply_disclaimer_accepted_at`), not the application — recorded with timestamp + IP in `audit_events` with `disclaimer_text_version` + `disclaimer_text_sha256` per the existing audit schema. Subsequent applies do not re-prompt unless the disclaimer text materially changes (a new version forces a one-time re-accept on next apply).
