.taskmaster\docs\prd.md:310: **Dependencies:** REQ-007 (Volunteer model), REQ-008 (GitHub integration)
.taskmaster\docs\prd.md:355: - [ ] Issue status is deterministic: self-assignment marks "in progress" (the commitment signal — the dev's pull); PR merge via Linear's GitHub integration marks "done"; agents comment and self-assign but never move status (detect-and-revert enforces, REQ-026). The working discipline is **pull-then-complete, and the Claude Code Skill (REQ-028) enforces it (decision-24(b))**: the dev pulls an issue (or explicitly enters the exploration bucket) before substantial work — so every metered request carries attribution context — and completion is an explicit dev act: the dev marks work done, and the Skill verifies and drives the merge path that flips status. The project's % complete = `done_p0 / total_p0` from the projection.
